{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"21a0b1a5-9af4-4e2f-b35c-4a8701bc1a11","status":"SUCCESS","response":"**ANSWER.md** – see the file created in the artifact directory.\n\nThe fix addressed the three root causes identified from the colleague’s note:\n\n1. **Init endpoint was a GET link** – converted to an authenticated **POST** that returns JSON `{ \"authorize_url\": … }`. The frontend now uses `fetch` POST to obtain the URL and redirects with `window.location.assign`.  \n2. **Duplicate scopes** – cleaned up `SCOPES` to list each area only once and only the needed `:WRITE` scopes, eliminating the “Duplicate scope” error.  \n3. **Token expiry handling** – the Intervals token never expires and has no `refresh_token`. Updated `store_connection` to set a far‑future expiry (10 years) when no refresh token is present and skip the periodic refresh logic.\n\n**Files changed**\n- `server.py` – POST‑only auth init, removed GET handling, added comments, updated `store_connection` expiry logic.  \n- `config.py` – fixed `SCOPES` to avoid duplicate entries.  \n- `static/app.js` – replaced the static `\u003ca\u003e` link with a POST‑fetch flow that injects a “Connect” button dynamically.  \n- `ANSWER.md` – documents the causes, applied fixes, and remaining work.\n","duration_seconds":263.106007,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":51721,"output_tokens":25140,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":763392,"total_tokens":76861}}}
